# Go packages whose Node code changed without the port, one per line (names
# from gateway/node-map.json). A PR that changes Node behavior a port mirrors
# either updates the port in gateway/ or lists the package here, and
# scripts/gateway-drift-check.mjs accepts that. The gateway embeds this list
# (gateway/files.go): every mapped package is on the native /v1/messages
# path, so any listed one, or any name that isn't a package, keeps that whole
# route proxied to Node until the port catches up (docs/GO_GATEWAY.md, Risks).
# Lines starting with # are comments.
